expr main [(per my last email), (as per my last email), (per my previous email), (as per my previous email)]

let message "`Per my last email` can read as passive-aggressive. Try a neutral reminder."
let description "Suggests warmer, clearer wording than `per my last email` in emails."
let kind "Style"
let becomes ["as discussed earlier", "as I said in my last email"]

# True positives
test "We think per my last email the plan is solid." "We think as discussed earlier the plan is solid."
test "My manager said as per my last email the budget." "My manager said as discussed earlier the budget."
test "She wrote per my previous email the summary." "She wrote as discussed earlier the summary."
test "After the call, as per my previous email the team agreed." "After the call, as discussed earlier the team agreed."
test "Maybe per my last email the results will help." "Maybe as discussed earlier the results will help."
test "We think as per my last email the plan is solid." "We think as discussed earlier the plan is solid."
test "My manager said per my previous email the budget." "My manager said as discussed earlier the budget."
test "She wrote as per my previous email the summary." "She wrote as discussed earlier the summary."
test "Honestly, per my last email this is fine." "Honestly, as discussed earlier this is fine."
test "Per my last email the plan." "As discussed earlier the plan."

# True negatives
allows "As I mentioned earlier, the file is ready."
allows "My last email had the file."
allows "Per the contract, we pay monthly."
allows "She wrote an email last week."
allows "Per diem rates apply."
allows "See my previous message."
allows "The report is ready."
